larmorx-gpl holds bit-exact replicas of GPL-licensed neuroimaging tools: Rust translations of
their source code. It is free software, licensed under the GNU General Public License,
version 3 or (at your option) any later version (see LICENSE). It comes with ABSOLUTELY NO
WARRANTY. Its source code is published at https://github.com/karellopez/larmorx (directory
crates-gpl/). Each translated file names its licence in an SPDX header and its origin in a
comment; each crate's PROVENANCE.md lists the upstream files it was translated from and the
changes made.

The program is a separate work from larmorx (Apache-2.0), which runs it as a separate process
when it is installed. It does not present itself as AFNI or as any other upstream tool.


